    {
      "panel_type": "story",
      "panel_label": "panel 4 ",
      "poster": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/poster/poster1_1x.webp",
      "message": [
        {
          "message_id": 1,
          "user": {
            "avatar": "girl"
          },
          "message_text": "Plants are unique because they can make their own food using water, carbon dioxide, and minerals from their surroundings.",
          "audio": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg1_ana.mp3",
          "audio_trans": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg1_ana_trans.json"
        },
        {
          "user": {
            "avatar": "boy"
          },
          "message_text": "Oh, so that’s why they don’t need to eat other organisms!",
          "audio": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg2_roger.mp3",
          "audio_trans": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg2_roger_trans.json"
        },
        {
          "user": {
            "avatar": "girl"
          },
          "message_text": "Correct! This process is called autotrophic nutrition. Auto means self, and trophos means nourishment. So, plants are autotrophs because they nourish themselves.",
          "audio": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg3_ana.mp3",
          "audio_trans": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl4/msg3_ana_trans.json"
        }
      ],
      "question": [
        {
          "panel_type": "question",
          "question_type": "boolean",
          "text": "Animals are also capable of autotrophic nutrition.",
          "options": [
            {
              "title": "True",
              "value": "True"
            },
            {
              "title": "False",
              "value": "False"
            }
          ],
          "answer": "False",
          "audio": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "panel_type": "story",
      "panel_label": "panel 5",
      "poster": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl5/poster/poster1_1x.webp",
      "message": [
        {
          "user": {
            "avatar": "boy"
          },
          "message_text": "That makes sense. And since animals can’t make their own food, we depend on plants or other animals that eat plants, right?",
          "audio_trans": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl5/msg1_roger_trans.json",
          "audio": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl5/msg1_roger.mp3"
        },
        {
          "message_id": 1,
          "user": {
            "avatar": "girl"
          },
          "message_text": "Exactly! Since animals eat plants or plant-eaters, they are called Heterotrophs. (heteros = other)",
          "audio": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl5/msg2_ana.mp3",
          "audio_trans": "https://toby-app-dev-ui.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/assert/frames/cbse/7std/science/chpt1/blk1/pnl5/msg2_ana_trans.json"
        }
      ],
      "question": [
        {
          "panel_type": "question",
          "question_type": "fillup",
          "text": "Since animals cannot make their own food, they depend on plants or other animals, making them _______.",
          "options": [
            {
              "title": "heterotrophs",
              "value": "heterotrophs"
            },
            {
              "title": "autotrophs",
              "value": "autotrophs"
            }
          ],
          "answer": "heterotrophs",
          "audio": ""
        }
      ]
